Z||000000||jlhuber||01-30-2001||09:56 PM||||I think this has been covered before, but I am unable to find it with the search function.  With the '96 & up 3800 series II supercharged motor with the 4spd auto stuffed into a '86-'88 GT, what kind of performance numbers could I expect?  What are you guys that have already done this swap getting for 0-60s and 1/4s?  How about gas mileage?<P>TIA<P>------------------<BR>--Jess--<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/blackeye2/double0smile.gif">  <BR>Speed costs money, how fast you wanna go?||||reg||1
Z||000001||BENGAL4||01-30-2001||10:30 PM||||My swap is almost completed. I have a 1997 3800 Series II S/C. The numbers are 250 hp and 280 ft lbs of torque. No performance numbers yet, but I'm sure there are a few members that can supply the info.<P>Bill||||reg||1
